{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487404853,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDg2MjM0Mzg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1313","origin":"github"},"title":"Strategies for reobtaining data on `update` (follow up on #101)","message":"With #1304 `update` now has `--reobtain-data`, which maintains content availability on a per-file basis when upgrading. A possible extension could be to have some sort of `--reobtain-data-strategy` option that is set to 'file' by default (current behavior), but different strategies are available. Here is a list of potentially interesting ones:\n\n- 'files': current behavior\n- 'directories-complete': obtain content of all files in all directories that had all files with content prior update (originally suggested in #101)\n- 'directories-new': gets anything new in any directory that had any file with content prior update\n- 'new': get content for anything new in the entire dataset\n\nAll three new ones should be relatively straightforward to implement in the present `update`, by amending the filtering of the list of files with content that is already produced.","files":null}]}